# A Unified Multi-Modal System for Image Forgery, Text Plagiarism, and AI-Generated Content Detection

A digital forensics web platform built on Django. It combines **Dual-Stream Vision Transformer (ViT-B/16) + DenseNet-121** (with Error Level Analysis) for image tampering localization and **RAG-based Semantic Vector Retrieval (ChromaDB + SentenceTransformers) + Local LLM Attribution** for academic plagiarism verification.

---

## 1. System Architecture & Workflows

### Text Plagiarism Detection (RAG Pipeline)

```
Uploaded Document (.PDF / .TXT)
   │
   ▼
[PyMuPDF Multi-Column Block Sorting]
   │
   ▼
[Sentence Splitter & Text Normalization]
   │
   ▼
[all-MiniLM-L6-v2 Embeddings] (users/models/sentence_transformer_model/)
   │
   ▼
[ChromaDB Persistent Vector Search] (users/chroma_db/ vs. users/data/ieee_papers/)
   │
   ├─► Cosine Distance < 0.35 (Similarity >= 65%) ──► Flag Match
   │
   ▼
[Ollama Qwen 2.5 LLM Attribution Engine]
   │
   ▼
Dynamic PDF Report Generation (ReportLab) + SQLite History Log

```

### Image Forgery Detection (Dual-Stream Pipeline)

```
Uploaded Image (.JPG / .PNG / .TIF)
   │
   ├─► Stream 1: RGB Image ────────────► ViT-B/16 (Global Semantic Context)
   │                                           │
   ├─► Stream 2: ELA (Residual Map) ───► DenseNet-121 (Compression Noise Artifacts)
   │                                           │
   ▼                                           ▼
[Cross-Attention Multi-Head Fusion + Squeeze-and-Excitation (SE)]
   │
   ▼
Binary Classification Head (Authentic vs. Tampered Probability)
   │
   ▼
Explainable Forensic Diagnostic + Side-by-Side ELA Visualizer

```

