## 2. Directory Layout

Verify your project layout matches the structure below before running on a new machine:

```text
App/
├── manage.py
├── db.sqlite3
├── static/                                 <-- Static assets directory
│
├── model/                                  <-- Image Forgery PyTorch Weights
│   ├── vit_densenet_forgery_detector.pth   <-- Ensure this .pth file is placed here
│   ├── model_metadata.json
│   └── test_metadata.csv
│
├── Templates/
│   └── users/
│       ├── userimageforgery.html           <-- Image Scanner UI & ELA Viewer
│       ├── forgery_history.html            <-- Paginated Image History Table
│       ├── userplagrism.html               <-- Text Scanner UI & PDF Downloader
│       └── plagiarism_history.html         <-- Paginated Plagiarism History Table
│
├── unifiedmodel/
│   ├── settings.py
│   ├── urls.py
│   └── wsgi.py
│
└── users/
    ├── apps.py                             <-- Server startup hook
    ├── models.py                           <-- PlagiarismCheck & ImageForgeryCheck schemas
    ├── urls.py                             <-- App routing
    ├── views.py                            <-- Controller endpoints & PDF handlers
    │
    ├── data/
    │   └── ieee_papers/                    <-- Reference IEEE base papers (*.pdf)
    │
    ├── chroma_db/                          <-- Persistent ChromaDB vector index
    │
    ├── models/                             <-- Local Model Storage Cache
    │   ├── sentence_transformer_model/     <-- MiniLM weights (auto-saved)
    │   └── ollama_models/                  <-- Ollama GGUF storage (auto-routed)
    │
    └── services/
        ├── indexer_service.py              <-- PyMuPDF extraction & ChromaDB vectorizer
        ├── rag_detector.py                 <-- Sentence search & similarity scoring
        ├── ollama_service.py               <-- Qwen 2.5 local reasoning & attribution
        ├── forgery_detector.py             <-- Dual-Stream PyTorch inference & ELA
        └── report_generator.py             <-- ReportLab PDF document compiler

```

