## 3. Installation & Setup

### Step 1: Clone / Copy Project & Create Virtual Environment

```bash
# Windows (PowerShell)
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Linux / macOS
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

```

### Step 2: Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install django torch torchvision torchaudio sentence-transformers chromadb pymupdf nltk reportlab ollama pillow numpy matplotlib

```

### Step 3: Configure Ollama (Local LLM Reasoning)

1. Download and install Ollama from [ollama.com/download](https://ollama.com/download).
2. Start the Ollama background daemon:
```bash
ollama serve

```


3. Pull the Qwen model (optional; the Django startup hook will download it automatically if `ollama serve` is active):
```bash
ollama pull qwen2.5:7b

```



### Step 4: Run Migrations & Launch Server

```bash
python manage.py makemigrations users
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py runserver

```

---

## 4. Maintenance & Reset Commands

### Reset & Rebuild ChromaDB Vector Index

Run this if reference papers in `users/data/ieee_papers/` are modified, deleted, or corrupted:

```powershell
# Windows (PowerShell)
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "users\chroma_db"

# Linux / macOS
rm -rf users/chroma_db

```

*Restarting `python manage.py runserver` will re-index all papers with layout sorting.*

### Force Re-download of SentenceTransformer Weights

```powershell
# Windows (PowerShell)
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "users\models\sentence_transformer_model"

# Linux / macOS
rm -rf users/models/sentence_transformer_model

```

