## 5. Troubleshooting & Debugging Guide

| Issue / Error Message | Root Cause | Fix / Resolution |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `[Errno 2] No such file or directory` during paper indexing | **Windows 260-Character `MAX_PATH` Limit**.<br>

<br>Long file titles in deep paths exceed Windows API limits. | `to_windows_long_path()` in `indexer_service.py` prepends `\\?\` to bypass path length limits. Ensure all file operations pass through this helper. |
| `[Ollama Note] Failed to connect to Ollama` | **Ollama Daemon Offline**.<br>

<br>The background service is not running. | Run `ollama serve` in a background terminal. The system automatically falls back to vector similarity scoring if Ollama is unreachable. |
| `FileNotFoundError: model/vit_densenet_forgery_detector.pth` | **Missing Checkpoint Path**.<br>

<br>Weights are missing or misplaced. | Ensure `vit_densenet_forgery_detector.pth` is placed in `App/model/` (the root model folder, not `App/users/models/`). |
| Low similarity score (e.g., 40%) on an identical document | **Layout Fragmentation**.<br>

<br>Standard `pypdf` reading two-column papers line-by-line. | Use `pymupdf` with `get_text("blocks", sort=True)` (already implemented in `indexer_service.py` and `views.py`). Wipe `users/chroma_db` once to rebuild. |
| `An embedding function already exists... Embedding function conflict` | **ChromaDB Metadata Mismatch**.<br>

<br>Embedding function changed without resetting cache. | Delete `users/chroma_db/` and run `python manage.py runserver` to recreate the collection. |
| `WARNINGS: ?: (staticfiles.W004) directory .../static does not exist` | **Missing Static Folder** | Run `mkdir static` in the root `App/` directory. |
| `Torch CUDA out of memory` / `Device Assertion Error` | **VRAM Exhaustion**.<br>

<br>GPU lacks dedicated memory for dual-stream batch inference. | The script defaults to CPU if CUDA is unavailable. Force CPU fallback in `users/services/forgery_detector.py` by setting `device = torch.device("cpu")`. |
| `PermissionError: [WinError 32] The process cannot access the file` | **File Locking**.<br>

<br>A running Python process or SQLite database instance locked the vector files. | Stop all running Django servers and kill background tasks via PowerShell: `Get-Process python | Stop-Process -Force`. |

